 800          * \brief
 801          *  This function is called to execute the following algorithm:
 802          *
 803          * -    Validate the Bootloadable application for the Classic Single-app Bootloader or 
 804          *   both Bootloadable/Combination applications for the Classic Dual-app Bootloader/
 805          *   Launch-only Bootloader (Launcher for short) respectively.
 806          *  
 807          * -    For the Classic Single-app Bootloader: if the Bootloadable application is valid, 
 808          *   then the flow switches to it after a software reset. Otherwise it stays in 
 809          *   the Bootloader, waiting for a command(s) from the host.
 810          * 
 811          * -    For the Classic Dual-app Bootloader: the flow acts according to the switching table 
 812          *  (see in the code below) and enabled/disabled options (for instance, auto-switching).
 813          *   NOTE If the valid Bootloadable application is identified, then the control is passed 
 814          *   to it after a software reset. Otherwise it stays in the Classic Dual-app Bootloader 
 815          *   waiting for a command(s) from the host.
 816          * 
 817          * -    For the Launcher: the flow acts according to the switching table (see below) and 
 818          *   enabled/disabled options. NOTE If the valid Combination application is identified, then 
 819          *   the control is passed to it after a software reset. Otherwise it stays in the Launcher 
 820          *   forever.
 821          * 
 822          * -    Validate the Bootloader/Launcher application(s) (design-time configurable, Bootloader 
 823          *   application validation option of the component customizer).
 824          * 
 825          * -    Run a communication subroutine (design-time configurable, the Wait for command 
 826          *   option of the component customizer). NOTE This is NOT applicable for the Launcher.
 827          *
 828          * -    Schedule the Bootloadable and reset the device.
 829          *
 830          *  \ref page_switching_logic
 831          *
 832          * \return
 833          *  This method will never return. It will either load a new application and
 834          *  reset the device or jump directly to the existing application. The CPU is
 835          *  halted, if the validation fails when the "Bootloader application validation" 
 836          *  option is enabled.
 837          *  PSoC 3/PSoC 5: The CPU is halted if flash initialization fails.
 838          *
 839          * \details
